namespace FlexFlow {
/**

@page run-model run-model

\brief Run the model specified by the \ref MappedParallelComputationGraph, encoded as JSON.

The main entry point for the FlexFlow Train model runner. The runner takes a \ref MappedParallelComputationGraph generated by \ref lib/compiler and runs it on a (potentially distributed, potentially heterogeneous) machine via the Realm runtime layer.

\verbatim
$ proj cmake # if you haven't already
...
$ proj build
...
$ proj run -- run-model -h
\endverbatim

The above should print the help message for `run-model`.

A typical workflow would involve generating a model's \ref ComputationGraph (e.g., via \ref export-model-arch) and then compiling it (via \ref compile-model) to a \ref MappedParallelComputationGraph before running:

\verbatim
$ proj run -- export-model-arch split_test > split_test_cg.json
$ proj run -- compile-model split_test_cg.json split_test_mpcg.json passthrough
$ proj run -- run-model split_test_mpcg.json
\endverbatim

*/
}
